      "author": "Akshay",
      "description": "On-demand SSH/SFTP server (dropbear, repackaged from notmarek/kindle-usbnetlite) over your existing WiFi — no USB networking needed. A random password is generated on install and printed in the KPM log; set your own any time by editing /mnt/us/usbnetlite/etc/ssh_password and restarting the server. Verified working end-to-end (install, launch, real SSH session, survives upgrade/downgrade) on Kindle PaperWhite 4, kernel 4.1.x.",
